\begin_layout Standard

\emph on
TSP is not limited to physical distances,
 but any other optimization function in place of the distance can be used.
 In the early days,
 travel distance or travel time were used (Dantzig and Ramser,
 1959),
 but currently,
 other objectives also exist,
 such as minimizing the exposure to sunlight (Li et al.,
 2019),
 maximizing the safety of travel (Krumm and Horvitz,
 2017),
 or minimizing CO2 levels (Kuo and Wang,
 2011;
 Lin et al.,
 2014).
 Practical applications include logistics such as vacation planning or orienteering (Fränti et al.,
 2017),
 transportation of goods,
 providing maintenance,
 or offering health services (Golden et al.,
 2008),
 among others.
\end_layout

